A program may contain millions of instructions, but typically only a small fraction of them execute frequently. Profiling studies consistently show that most execution time is concentrated in loops. Consequently, optimisers invest heavily in loop transformations: they are high-payoff, they compose well with each other, and they are relatively safe when applied correctly.

